<newsitem itemid="769237" id="root" date="1997-07-31" xml:lang="en">
<title>CHINA: Rivera yearly net returns to blacks.</title>
<headline>Rivera yearly net returns to blacks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>     Shr (H.K. cents)	 0.5 gain    vs 2.4 loss</p>
<p>     Dividend (H.K. cents)  nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>     Exceptional itmes	nil	   vs 30.14 loss</p>
<p>     Net			  6.69 profit vs 30.47 loss (see note)</p>
<p>     Turnover		   2.30	  vs 2.22</p>
<p>     Company name	     Rivera (Holdings) Ltd</p>
<p>     Books close		Sept 15-24</p>
<p>     Dividend payable	 N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - Rivera is an investment holding company with subsidiaries engaged in property investment, securities trading and investment holding.</p>
<p>Net is after share of profit from associated companies of HK$23.40 million during the period under review compared with HK$18.59 million a year ago.</p>
<p>The company proposes a bonus issue of one 2000 warrant for every five shares held. The warrant entitles holder the right to subscribe one new company share at HK$0.50 each before expiry on April 30, 2000.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6370</p>
</text>
